        "explanation": "Setting `\"strict\": true` in your `tsconfig.json` enables a wide range of rigorous type-checking behaviors. It represents the gold standard for how TypeScript should be written. It turns on several underlying flags simultaneously, including:\n- `noImplicitAny`: Errors if TS has to guess 'any' for a type.\n- `strictNullChecks`: Prevents assigning `null`/`undefined` to variables unless explicitly allowed.\n- `strictBindCallApply`: Ensures arguments passed to `bind`, `call`, and `apply` are strictly typed.\n- `strictPropertyInitialization`: Ensures class properties are initialized in the constructor.",
