        "category": "TypeScript Fundamentals",
        "language": "typescript",
        "explanation": "Type Narrowing is the process where TypeScript analyzes your control flow (if/else statements, switch statements) to automatically refine a broad type (like `string | number`) into a more specific, narrower type (like just `string`). \nThis allows you to safely call methods on a variable that were previously unsafe.",
