        "explanation": "This is inherited from ES6 JavaScript:\n1. **`var`:** Function-scoped. It suffers from 'hoisting' (can be accessed before declaration resulting in `undefined`) and can be re-declared in the same scope. Very bug-prone.\n2. **`let`:** Block-scoped `{}`. It can be reassigned but cannot be re-declared in the same scope. Safe for variables that change (loops, counters).\n3. **`const`:** Block-scoped `{}`. Cannot be reassigned. The binding is immutable (though objects/arrays assigned to it can still have their contents mutated).",
