        "explanation": "Rest parameters allow a function to accept an indefinite (unlimited) number of arguments as an array. You define them using the ES6 spread syntax `...` before the parameter name. \nIn TypeScript, the type of a rest parameter MUST be defined as an array type (e.g., `string[]` or `number[]`).",
