        "explanation": "Arrow functions are a concise syntax for writing function expressions in ES6 JavaScript. They are heavily used in modern TS/JS frameworks. \nTheir defining feature (besides shorter syntax) is that they **do not have their own `this` binding**; they inherit `this` from the surrounding lexical scope, eliminating many bugs related to callbacks and object methods.",
