        "title": "What is function overloading?",
        "category": "TypeScript Fundamentals",
        "language": "typescript",
        "explanation": "Function Overloading allows you to define multiple distinct type signatures for a single function. This is highly useful when a function can accept different types of arguments and return different types based on those arguments. \nYou write multiple signature definitions (without bodies) followed by ONE actual implementation that handles all the logic and uses broad types (`any` or unions).",
