        "language": "typescript",
        "explanation": "They are two different module systems in the JS ecosystem:\n1. **CommonJS (CJS):** The original standard used by Node.js. Uses `require()` for imports and `module.exports` for exports. It is **synchronous**.\n2. **ES Modules (ESM):** The modern, official standard for JavaScript (used in browsers and modern Node). Uses `import` and `export`. It is **asynchronous** and statically analyzable (which allows bundlers to 'Tree Shake' / remove dead code).\nTypeScript allows you to write ESM (`import/export`) and will automatically transpile it to CJS (`require`) if configured to do so.",
