        "explanation": "Control Flow Analysis (CFA) is the incredibly sophisticated underlying engine in the TypeScript compiler that tracks the type of a variable as it flows through logical branches (`if`, `switch`, `return`, `throw`, `catch`). \nBecause of CFA, a variable's type can physically change on every single line of code depending on what runtime checks you have performed on it.",
