        "explanation": "Type Compatibility dictates whether you can assign one variable to another. Because TypeScript uses a structural type system (Duck Typing), X is compatible with Y if Y has at least the same members as X. \nWhen checking compatibility, TypeScript ignores the names of the types and deeply compares their internal structure.",
