        "category": "Advanced TypeScript",
        "language": "typescript",
        "explanation": "Variadic Tuple Types (introduced in TS 4.0) allow you to use the spread operator (`...`) *inside* a tuple type definition, spreading generic arrays or other tuples into it. \nThis allows you to mathematically model functions that take an unknown number of arguments (like `concat` or currying functions) while preserving strict types at every single index.",
