        "explanation": "In JavaScript, the `this` keyword is dynamic and notorious for changing context. \nTypeScript allows you to strictly enforce what `this` must be when a function is called by declaring a fake parameter named `this` as the **very first parameter** of the function signature. The compiler uses this to ensure the function is only called on the correct object.",
