        "explanation": "- **Abstract Methods:** Methods declared in an `abstract` class without a body. They *force* the child class to implement them. They provide no default behavior.\n- **Virtual Methods:** A concept from C#/Java. They are methods with a default implementation in the parent class that *can* be optionally overridden by the child class. \nIn TypeScript/JavaScript, **ALL** normal methods are inherently 'virtual' by default, meaning they can always be overridden.",
